# New Dawn — Build Playbook v1 (plan + Claude Code prompts)

_Written 2026-10-23. Companion to `plan.md` (architecture), `ai-engine.md` (AI design) and `meetily-teardown.md` (reference code). Decisions locked here: app name **New Dawn**; typeface **Be Vietnam Pro** everywhere, for every tenant; a tenant may customise only **logo, colours, corner-radius style and button style**; bundle id **`co.majorisdigital.newdawn`** (fixed from Phase 1 on)._

> **Status 2026-10-23:** the scaffold and the §2 files are already in this repo. Follow `GETTING_STARTED.md` for the toolchain steps, then start at **P0**.

## 0. How to use this playbook

- Work in order. Each **prompt** is one Claude Code session and ends with something you can open. Never merge two prompts into one.
- Every prompt follows the loop: **THINK** (you read the prompt) → **ALIGN** (Claude Code summarises its plan in ≤ 10 bullets and waits for your "go") → **SEE** (for UI prompts it first makes a quick static mockup screen) → **BUILD**.
- After every prompt: `/build-check`, read `LAST_BUILD.md`, commit. If `cargo check` is red, ask Claude Code to explain each error in one plain sentence before fixing.
- The reference code lives at `../Ref/meetily` (clone command in `GETTING_STARTED.md`). Prompts say "port from Meetily `path`" — that means *read it, rewrite it cleanly*, never copy files wholesale.

## 1. Phase 0 — set-up checklist

See `GETTING_STARTED.md` (Terminal steps in order). Done when: the hello window opens in Be Vietnam Pro, `cargo check` in `src-tauri/` is clean, `ollama list` shows both Qwen models, `../Ref/meetily` exists.

## 2. Repo scaffolding (already in place)

`CLAUDE.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, `LAST_BUILD.md`, `.claude/agents/{architect-reviewer,migration-safety}.md`, `.claude/commands/build-check.md`, `.claude/skills/newdawn-ui-patterns/SKILL.md`, `docs/`, `brands/`, `scripts/check-localhost-only.sh`, `src/styles/{tokens,base}.css`, `src-tauri/{tauri.conf.json, .cargo/config.toml, Info.plist, entitlements.plist}`.

## 3. Prompt template and ground rules

Every prompt below is pasted into Claude Code verbatim. They all start the same way:

> Read `CLAUDE.md`, then the sections of `docs/` named below. Summarise your plan in ≤ 10 bullets — files you will create or change, crates/packages you will add, and anything you are unsure of — then wait for my "go" before writing any code. When you add a crate, check its current API on docs.rs before using it; do not guess signatures.

And end the same way:

> When done: run `/build-check`, update `LAST_BUILD.md` and `DECISIONS.md`, run the `architect-reviewer` agent, and list the exact manual steps I must do (e.g. grant a permission, copy a file).

If Claude Code proposes something that breaks a CLAUDE.md rule, say "that breaks rule N, redo". If it gets stuck in a compile-error loop for more than ~3 rounds on the same error, stop and ask it to explain the error in plain words and propose two different fixes.

