#### P1.2 — Registry, WorkspaceHub, migrations, typed bridge

```
Read CLAUDE.md "Architecture rules" and "Database conventions", docs/plan.md §4 and §9. Goal: workspaces exist as real files.

Build:
1. Add `sqlx` (runtime-tokio, sqlite, uuid, chrono), `uuid` (v7), `tokio`, `anyhow`, `thiserror`, `tracing`, `tracing-subscriber`, `tauri-specta` + `specta`, `trash`. Create `src-tauri/src/error.rs` (`AppError` with `code` + `message`, `From` for sqlx/io/anyhow, serialises for commands).
2. `migrations/registry/0001_init.sql`: `workspace` (id, slug UNIQUE, name, folder_path, brand_ref, enabled_modules JSON, archived INTEGER, last_opened_at, created_at, updated_at), `setting` (key PRIMARY KEY, value JSON). `migrations/workspace/0001_init.sql`: `project`, `task`, `note` per docs/plan.md §9 plus FTS5 tables for task.title/notes_md and note.title/body_md with sync triggers. (Meetings, entities, research come in later migrations.)
