Investigate and note in DECISIONS: whether this whisper-rs version exposes whisper.cpp's built-in Silero VAD (would remove the `ort` dependency); whether the Core ML encoder (`ggml-large-v3-turbo-encoder.mlmodelc`) is worth bundling on this M1 Pro (measure a 10-minute file both ways).
Done when: a 30-minute m4a from Voice Memos imports with a visible progress bar and produces a readable, timestamped English transcript; the memory scheduler shows Whisper loaded/unloaded correctly.
```

#### P3c-i — Recorder foundation: permissions, microphone, incremental save

```
Read docs/plan.md §10 Phase 3c, docs/meetily-teardown.md §2.7, reference ../Ref/meetily/frontend/src-tauri/src/audio/{stream.rs, pipeline.rs (mic path only), incremental_saver.rs, permissions.rs, devices/discovery.rs}. Build `src-tauri/src/recorder/` step one:
1. Confirm Info.plist usage descriptions and the single `device.audio-input` entitlement; `kernel/permissions.rs` with check/request for microphone (trigger a cpal stream to raise the TCC prompt) and a "System Audio Recording" explainer that opens the right System Settings pane.
2. `recorder/mic.rs`: `cpal` default input, F32/I16 handling, resample to 48 kHz mono via `rubato`, 80 Hz high-pass, EBU R128 loudness to −23 LUFS (`ebur128`); pushes 100 ms frames into a **bounded** channel (capacity 50) and counts drops.
3. `recorder/saver.rs`: incremental 16 kHz mono WAV writer (header patched on finalize), flush every 2 s, recovers a truncated file on next launch.
4. `recorder/session.rs`: state machine Idle → Recording → Paused → Stopping → Idle; `start(workspace, title)`, `pause`, `resume`, `stop`; emits `recorder-state` and `recorder-level` (RMS, 10 Hz) events.
5. UI: the toolbar Record pill becomes live (● / elapsed / level meter / ■), ⌘R, menu-bar item; a "Permissions" step in Settings → General with status pills.
Done when: pressing ● records my voice to a WAV under the current workspace's attachments, the level meter moves, pausing works, and killing the app mid-recording leaves a playable file.
```

#### P3c-ii — System audio via Core Audio process tap + mixer

```
Read docs/meetily-teardown.md §2.7 and §6 (items 5, 10), reference ../Ref/meetily/frontend/src-tauri/src/audio/capture/{core_audio.rs, system.rs, backend_config.rs} and audio/pipeline.rs `mix_window`. Build:
1. `recorder/system_tap.rs` with the `cidre` crate: a global mono process tap (`TapDesc::with_mono_global_tap_excluding_processes`) in a private aggregate device with tap auto-start; 1024-sample blocks into a bounded channel; detect the "permission denied → silence" case (all-zero frames for 3 s while the mic level meter is active) and report it.
2. `recorder/mixer.rs`: align mic and system streams in 600 ms windows via a ring buffer, mix = sum with proportional soft scaling above ±1 (no ducking), expose per-source levels.
3. Session: mixed stream feeds the saver; UI level meter shows two bars (you / them); a "System audio permission" banner if the tap returns silence.
Done when: during a Zoom/Meet test call the WAV contains both sides cleanly, with no echo and no clipping.
```

#### P3c-iii — Live voice detection, Whisper worker, live transcript

```
Read docs/ai-engine.md §3a (VAD, worker) and docs/meetily-teardown.md §2.5, §6 items 9–10; reference ../Ref/meetily/frontend/src-tauri/src/audio/{vad.rs, transcription/worker.rs, transcription/engine.rs}. Build:
1. `recorder/vad.rs`: Silero on the mixed stream resampled to 16 kHz with `rubato` (not a moving average), redemption 500 ms live, pads 300/400, min 250; emits speech segments; a maximum segment length of 30 s (force-cut at the quietest 100 ms window).
2. `recorder/worker.rs`: one Whisper worker reading a **bounded** segment queue (capacity 8); when the queue is full the oldest segment is written to a "catch-up" list transcribed after Stop, and the UI shows a lag indicator; each segment → `transcript-update {seq, start_ms, end_ms, text}`; segments persisted as they arrive (source = live).
3. Stop: flush VAD, drain queue, transcribe catch-up list with progress, finalise meeting row; the memory scheduler keeps Whisper loaded during a recording and unloads after.
4. UI: live transcript pane in the meeting page (auto-scroll, click pauses scroll), lag indicator, "Recording ended — N segments catching up".
Done when: a 20-minute test call shows text within a few seconds of speech on the M1 Pro, nothing is lost under load, and the final transcript equals the live one plus catch-up.
```

