## 5. Working rhythm (so it actually ships)

- One prompt per sitting; expect P1.x to take an evening each, P3c-ii and P3c-iii a weekend each.
- Keep `docs/journal.md`: date, prompt id, what worked, what surprised you. It becomes the DECISIONS feed.
- Start using the app for real at the end of P2.1 even though it is ugly in places; real use finds the right next prompt faster than planning does.
- If a prompt balloons past ~2 hours of fixing, stop, commit what compiles, and split the prompt — the playbook is a guide, not a contract.
